partialText:
&lt;h1&gt;


  Como aprendi Apache Spark — Parte 16: Apache Kafka, CDC e pipelines incrementais
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nota histórica: esta série revisita minha trajetória em Engenharia de Dados iniciada em 2012. Tecnologias como Structured Streaming, Debezium e os formatos Lakehouse modernos surgiram ou amadureceram posteriormente. Este capítulo conecta aquela experiência aos padrões atuais de integração de dados.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nos capítulos anteriores, construímos uma visão progressiva do Apache Spark.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Começamos pela execução distribuída, passamos por partições, shuffle, memória, otimização de consultas, armazenamento colunar, Lakehouse e qualidade de dados.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Na Parte 15, entramos no universo do Structured Streaming.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Aprendemos como o Spark processa fluxos de eventos utilizando microbatches, checkpoints, watermarks e gerenciamento de estado.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agora vamos responder a uma pergunta bastante comum em projetos corporativos:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Como manter uma plataforma analítica atualizada quando os dados estão mudando continuamente em sistemas transacionais?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine um e-commerce.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seu banco PostgreSQL recebe milhares de operações:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Novos pedidos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alterações de status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Atualizações cadastrais.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cancelamentos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exclusões.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma estratégia tradicional seria executar periodicamente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight sql"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;SELECT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;FROM&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pedidos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Mas, conforme a tabela cresce, reler todos os registros se torna cada vez mais caro.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Além disso, essa abordagem pode não identificar corretamente exclusões ou alterações intermediárias.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Precisamos de um mecanismo que permita capturar as mudanças.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;É aqui que entram &lt;strong&gt;Change Data Capture, Apache Kafka e Spark Structured Streaming&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Full Load vs. Incremental Load
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vamos começar pelo problema.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine uma tabela com 100 milhões de registros.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Todos os dias, apenas 200 mil registros são inseridos ou alterados.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma carga completa processaria:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;100,000,000 records
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Uma carga incremental poderia processar aproximadamente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;200,000 changed records
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A diferença potencial é significativa.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas precisamos entender como identificar as alterações.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma abordagem comum utiliza uma coluna como:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;updated_at
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Exemplo:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight sql"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;SELECT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;FROM&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pedidos&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;WHERE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;updated_at&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ultimo_processamento&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Esse mecanismo pode funcionar em determinados sistemas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Entretanto, possui limitações:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depende da atualização correta do timestamp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pode perder exclusões físicas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exige tratamento cuidadoso de empates e limites temporais.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pode perder alterações se o controle incremental for implementado incorretamente.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pode exigir consultas frequentes ao banco operacional.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma alternativa é capturar mudanças a partir do log transacional.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  2. O que é Change Data Capture?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change Data Capture (CDC)&lt;/strong&gt; é um conjunto de técnicas para identificar alterações realizadas em uma fonte de dados.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Essas alterações podem incluir:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;INSERT
UPDATE
DELETE
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Em vez de consultar repetidamente a tabela inteira, um mecanismo CDC pode observar as mudanças registradas pelo banco.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceitualmente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;              POSTGRESQL
                  |
                  v
           TRANSACTION LOG
                  |
                  v
              CDC ENGINE
                  |
                  v
             CHANGE EVENTS
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Existem diferentes implementações de CDC.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Algumas utilizam consultas periódicas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Outras utilizam logs de transação.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Neste artigo, vamos concentrar nossa atenção em CDC baseado em logs, especialmente com PostgreSQL e Debezium.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  3. PostgreSQL e Write-Ahead Log
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O PostgreSQL utiliza um mecanismo chamado &lt;strong&gt;Write-Ahead Logging (WAL)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O WAL registra informações necessárias à recuperação e à durabilidade das transações.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ele também pode ser utilizado, por meio de decodificação lógica, para disponibilizar alterações a sistemas externos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceitualmente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;SQL TRANSACTION
      |
      v
POSTGRESQL
      |
      v
     WAL
      |
      v
LOGICAL DECODING
      |
      v
CHANGE EVENTS
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A captura lógica exige configurações e permissões apropriadas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No PostgreSQL, isso envolve recursos como:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logical Replication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replication Slots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configurações de WAL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Controle de retenção.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma preocupação operacional importante é que replication slots podem reter WAL quando o consumidor não avança.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Se esse comportamento não for monitorado, o armazenamento do banco pode crescer significativamente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Portanto, CDC não é apenas uma configuração de integração.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;É também uma responsabilidade operacional.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  4. O papel do Debezium
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O &lt;strong&gt;Debezium&lt;/strong&gt; é uma plataforma de captura de alterações de bancos de dados.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma arquitetura comum utiliza Debezium com Kafka Connect.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;                  POSTGRESQL
                      |
                      v
                 LOGICAL WAL
                      |
                      v
                   DEBEZIUM
                      |
                      v
                 KAFKA CONNECT
                      |
                      v
                  KAFKA TOPIC
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;O Debezium interpreta alterações da origem e publica eventos estruturados.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dependendo da configuração, também pode executar um snapshot inicial dos dados antes de acompanhar as mudanças contínuas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Isso é importante.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Um novo pipeline CDC frequentemente precisa carregar o estado existente da tabela e depois continuar aplicando alterações.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Precisamos garantir que essa transição seja consistente.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  5. O que é Apache Kafka?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O Apache Kafka é uma plataforma distribuída de streaming de eventos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ele permite que produtores publiquem registros e consumidores os leiam.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceitualmente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;PRODUCERS
    |
    v
 KAFKA
    |
    +------ CONSUMER A
    |
    +------ CONSUMER B
    |
    +------ CONSUMER C
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Kafka oferece mecanismos para:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persistência de eventos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organização em tópicos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Particionamento.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replicação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leitura por offsets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consumo independente por diferentes aplicações.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas Kafka não é simplesmente uma fila tradicional.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seu modelo permite que consumidores acompanhem posições no log e, dentro das condições de retenção, releiam eventos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Essa característica é especialmente útil em arquiteturas de dados.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  6. Topics, Partitions e Offsets
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Um tópico Kafka pode ser dividido em partições.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;TOPIC: pedidos

Partition 0
[0] [1] [2] [3] [4]

Partition 1
[0] [1] [2] [3]

Partition 2
[0] [1] [2] [3] [4] [5]
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Cada partição possui sua própria sequência de offsets.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O offset identifica uma posição dentro daquela partição.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Portanto:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;partition = 0
offset = 10
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;e:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;partition = 1
offset = 10
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;representam posições diferentes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma propriedade importante é que Kafka preserva a ordem dos registros &lt;strong&gt;dentro de uma mesma partição&lt;/strong&gt;, não uma ordem global entre todas as partições.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Essa distinção influencia diretamente o processamento CDC.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  7. A importância da chave de particionamento
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine eventos de um pedido:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Pedido 101 → CRIADO
Pedido 101 → PAGO
Pedido 101 → ENVIADO
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Queremos preservar a sequência de alterações desse pedido.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma estratégia comum é utilizar:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pedido_id
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;como chave Kafka.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Isso normalmente faz com que eventos com a mesma chave sejam encaminhados à mesma partição, considerando um particionador e uma configuração estáveis.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas existem ressalvas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mudanças no número de partições, no particionador ou na estratégia de chave podem afetar essa propriedade ao longo do tempo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Além disso, a ordem do Kafka não substitui uma regra de versionamento dos eventos no destino.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em pipelines CDC, precisamos considerar tanto a ordem de transporte quanto a ordem lógica das alterações na origem.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  8. Consumer Groups
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Kafka permite organizar consumidores em grupos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dentro de um consumer group, as partições são distribuídas entre os consumidores participantes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceitualmente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;TOPIC: pedidos
     |
     +-- Partition 0 --&amp;gt; Consumer A
     |
     +-- Partition 1 --&amp;gt; Consumer B
     |
     +-- Partition 2 --&amp;gt; Consumer C
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Isso permite paralelismo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Entretanto, o número de partições limita o paralelismo efetivo de leitura por consumidores de um mesmo grupo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Se um tópico possui três partições, adicionar dez consumidores ao mesmo grupo não significa que todos receberão partições ativas simultaneamente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Também precisamos distinguir esse modelo da integração Spark.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O conector Kafka do Structured Streaming gerencia a leitura e o progresso da consulta utilizando seus próprios mecanismos de offsets e checkpoints.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Não devemos assumir que o gerenciamento de offsets de uma aplicação Spark seja idêntico ao de um consumidor Kafka convencional.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  9. Como é um evento CDC?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vamos considerar um evento simplificado inspirado na estrutura de envelopes Debezium.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"before"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"pedido_id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;101&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"status"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"CRIADO"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"valor"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;150.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"after"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"pedido_id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;101&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"status"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"PAGO"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"valor"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;150.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"op"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"u"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"ts_ms"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1793500000000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;O evento possui:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;before&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Estado anterior do registro, quando disponível.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;after&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Estado posterior do registro, quando aplicável.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;op&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tipo de operação.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ts_ms&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Timestamp associado ao evento, conforme a semântica do campo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em envelopes Debezium reais, também podemos encontrar informações adicionais sobre origem, transação e snapshots.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Os campos exatos dependem do conector, versão e configuração.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  10. Operações CDC
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em um envelope Debezium típico, podemos encontrar códigos como:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Código&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Significado&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;c&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Create / Insert&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;u&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Update&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;d&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Delete&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;r&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Read de snapshot&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O evento de snapshot merece atenção.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ele representa uma leitura do estado existente durante a inicialização ou uma operação de snapshot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Não deve ser tratado automaticamente como uma nova inserção de negócio.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A aplicação downstream precisa compreender a semântica desses eventos.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  11. DELETE e Tombstone
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Exclusões exigem cuidado especial.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Um evento de delete pode conter:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"before"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"pedido_id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;101&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"status"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"PAGO"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"after"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"op"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"d"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Dependendo da configuração Debezium/Kafka, também pode ser emitido um registro tombstone, com a chave do registro e valor Kafka nulo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Esse tombstone está relacionado à semântica de compactação de logs do Kafka.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ele não deve ser confundido com o evento CDC de exclusão.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma aplicação que simplesmente descarta mensagens de valor nulo precisa compreender o impacto dessa decisão.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;E uma aplicação que ignora eventos &lt;code&gt;d&lt;/code&gt; pode manter registros que já foram excluídos da origem.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  12. Arquitetura end-to-end
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vamos reunir os componentes.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;                  POSTGRESQL
                      |
                      v
                     WAL
                      |
                      v
                   DEBEZIUM
                      |
                      v
                 KAFKA CONNECT
                      |
                      v
                 KAFKA TOPIC
                      |
                      v
             SPARK STRUCTURED
                 STREAMING
                      |
                      v
               SCHEMA PARSING
                      |
                      v
               CDC NORMALIZATION
                      |
                      v
               DATA QUALITY
                      |
                      v
               INCREMENTAL MERGE
                      |
                      v
                LAKEHOUSE TABLE
                      |
                      v
                  SQL / BI / ML
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Cada camada possui responsabilidades específicas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O Debezium captura alterações.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Kafka transporta e retém eventos conforme sua configuração.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Spark interpreta, transforma e valida.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O formato Lakehouse gerencia o estado da tabela analítica.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Essa separação facilita a evolução da arquitetura.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  13. Lendo Kafka com Spark Structured Streaming
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vamos utilizar PySpark.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A integração exige o conector Kafka compatível com a versão do Spark e do Scala.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pyspark.sql&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;SparkSession&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;spark&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;SparkSession&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;appName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;SparkKafkaCDC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getOrCreate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_kafka&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;spark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;readStream&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;kafka&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;option&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;kafka.bootstrap.servers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;localhost:9092&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;option&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;subscribe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;dbserver1.public.pedidos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;option&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;startingOffsets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;earliest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;load&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;O endereço, o tópico e as configurações de segurança precisam corresponder ao ambiente real.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O parâmetro &lt;code&gt;startingOffsets&lt;/code&gt; define a posição inicial para uma nova consulta.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ao reiniciar uma consulta com checkpoint válido, o progresso persistido normalmente prevalece sobre essa configuração inicial.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  14. Interpretando o payload
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Kafka disponibiliza o valor da mensagem como binário.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Podemos convertê-lo para string:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pyspark.sql&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;functions&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;mensagens&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_kafka&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;cast&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;alias&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;kafka_key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;cast&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;alias&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;topic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;partition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;offset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;timestamp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Agora precisamos interpretar o JSON.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vamos definir um schema simplificado.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pyspark.sql.types&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;StructType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;LongType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;StringType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;DecimalType&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;schema_registro&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;LongType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StringType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;DecimalType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;schema_cdc&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;before&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;schema_registro&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;after&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;schema_registro&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;op&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StringType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;ts_ms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;LongType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Esse schema corresponde ao envelope simplificado apresentado anteriormente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em uma integração real, devemos ajustar o parsing à serialização utilizada, incluindo eventuais envelopes adicionais de Kafka Connect, formatos Avro ou Protobuf e integração com Schema Registry.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  15. Normalizando eventos CDC
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agora aplicamos &lt;code&gt;from_json&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_parseados&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;mensagens&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;withColumn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;cdc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;from_json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="n"&gt;schema_cdc&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Precisamos obter a chave do registro.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para INSERT e UPDATE, ela normalmente estará em &lt;code&gt;after&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para DELETE, pode estar em &lt;code&gt;before&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_normalizados&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_parseados&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;cdc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isNotNull&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;coalesce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;cdc.after.pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;cdc.before.pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;alias&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;cdc.after.status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;alias&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;cdc.after.valor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;alias&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;cdc.op&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;alias&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;operacao&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;cdc.ts_ms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;alias&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;event_ts_ms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;topic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;partition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;offset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Agora temos uma representação mais adequada para processamento incremental.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Entretanto, essa normalização ainda não resolve a ordenação lógica dos eventos.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  16. Por que timestamp não é suficiente para ordenar CDC?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine duas alterações do mesmo pedido:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Event A
pedido_id = 101
status = PAGO

Event B
pedido_id = 101
status = CANCELADO
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Se utilizarmos apenas um timestamp de baixa precisão, os eventos podem ter o mesmo valor temporal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Além disso, timestamps de processamento não representam necessariamente a ordem de commit na origem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para garantir a aplicação correta das alterações, devemos utilizar metadados de ordenação apropriados ao conector e ao banco.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No PostgreSQL, informações relacionadas à posição no WAL, como LSN, podem fazer parte dessa estratégia.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas é importante validar a semântica dos campos expostos pelo Debezium.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Não devemos assumir que um único campo de timestamp seja suficiente para reconstruir a ordem transacional em qualquer cenário.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  17. O problema dos eventos fora de ordem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Source Order:

1. CRIADO
2. PAGO
3. CANCELADO
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Mas o destino recebe ou aplica:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;1. CRIADO
2. CANCELADO
3. PAGO
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Se aplicarmos simplesmente a última mensagem recebida, o estado final ficará incorreto.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O pedido poderá aparecer como PAGO quando deveria estar CANCELADO.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Por isso, pipelines CDC precisam definir:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chave de negócio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ordenação lógica.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Estratégia de deduplicação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tratamento de eventos antigos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Política de reprocessamento.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A arquitetura precisa preservar ou reconstruir a sequência correta de alterações.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  18. Deduplicação por chave e versão
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vamos imaginar um dataset normalizado com:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pedido_id
status
valor
source_version
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Aqui, &lt;code&gt;source_version&lt;/code&gt; representa uma versão lógica de origem confiável, já normalizada e comparável dentro do domínio de cada pedido.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Não estamos assumindo que esse campo exista diretamente no envelope Debezium.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ele precisa ser construído conforme a semântica real da origem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Podemos selecionar a versão mais recente de cada pedido em um conjunto finito de eventos:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pyspark.sql&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Window&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pyspark.sql&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;functions&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;janela&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;Window&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;partitionBy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;orderBy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;desc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_recentes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;df_eventos&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;withColumn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;rn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;row_number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;over&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;janela&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;rn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;drop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;rn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Esse exemplo é adequado para um DataFrame batch, como o recebido dentro de &lt;code&gt;foreachBatch&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para resultados determinísticos, a ordenação precisa ser total ou possuir um critério de desempate definido.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Também precisamos tratar versões repetidas e eventos de delete.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  19. &lt;code&gt;foreachBatch&lt;/code&gt; para processamento incremental
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma estratégia comum é consumir eventos com Structured Streaming e aplicar cada microbatch ao destino.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;processar_microbatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;batch_df&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;batch_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Processando microbatch: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;batch_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Validar dados
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Normalizar operações
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Deduplicar eventos
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Aplicar MERGE transacional
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Iniciamos:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_normalizados&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;writeStream&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;foreachBatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;processar_microbatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;option&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;checkpointLocation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;/data/checkpoints/pedidos_cdc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;O checkpoint deve utilizar armazenamento persistente e adequado ao ambiente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Importante:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;foreachBatch&lt;/code&gt; oferece semântica de execução at-least-once para a função.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Se ocorrer uma falha, o mesmo microbatch pode ser executado novamente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Portanto, precisamos tornar a aplicação no destino idempotente.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  20. Upsert com MERGE INTO
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em um Lakehouse compatível, podemos aplicar atualizações incrementais com &lt;code&gt;MERGE&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Exemplo conceitual:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight sql"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;MERGE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;INTO&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lakehouse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sales&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;pedidos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;destino&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;USING&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pedidos_incrementais&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;ON&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;destino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;WHEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;MATCHED&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;AND&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;operacao&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'d'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;THEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;DELETE&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;WHEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;MATCHED&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;AND&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;operacao&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;IN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'c'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'u'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'r'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;THEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;UPDATE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;SET&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;destino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;destino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;WHEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;MATCHED&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;AND&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;operacao&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;IN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'c'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'u'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'r'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;THEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;INSERT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;VALUES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Esse exemplo demonstra a lógica básica de upsert e delete.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas ainda existe um problema.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Se um evento antigo chegar depois de um evento novo, o MERGE poderá sobrescrever o estado correto.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma implementação robusta deve comparar versões de origem e persistir a versão aplicada.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Além disso, uma exclusão precisa ser protegida contra a ressurreição indevida de registros por eventos antigos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dependendo dos requisitos, isso pode exigir tombstones lógicos ou uma tabela de controle de versões.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  21. Idempotência: não basta repetir o MERGE
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine que um microbatch seja aplicado com sucesso.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Antes de o Spark confirmar o progresso, ocorre uma falha.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Na recuperação, o mesmo microbatch é executado novamente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Se a operação for idempotente, o estado final permanecerá correto.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas precisamos avaliar:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se a fonte possui identificadores estáveis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se a versão da alteração é preservada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se operações antigas são ignoradas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se deletes são protegidos contra reintrodução.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se o destino oferece transações adequadas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se existem efeitos colaterais externos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Um &lt;code&gt;MERGE&lt;/code&gt; baseado apenas em chave pode não ser suficiente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A regra correta deve considerar a versão lógica da alteração.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  22. Exemplo de MERGE protegido por versão
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine uma tabela com:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pedido_id
status
valor
source_version
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Podemos utilizar uma condição adicional:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight sql"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;MERGE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;INTO&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lakehouse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sales&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;pedidos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;destino&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;USING&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pedidos_incrementais&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;ON&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;destino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;WHEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;MATCHED&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;AND&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;destino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;THEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;UPDATE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;SET&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;destino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;destino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;destino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;WHEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;MATCHED&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;THEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;INSERT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;VALUES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;origem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Essa estratégia demonstra a proteção contra atualizações antigas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Entretanto, o exemplo pressupõe eventos de inserção ou atualização e uma versão de origem confiável.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Deletes precisam de tratamento adicional, porque remover fisicamente o registro também remove a versão que impediria sua reintrodução por um evento atrasado.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em produção, a estratégia de exclusão deve ser projetada explicitamente.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  23. Snapshot inicial e streaming contínuo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Um desafio importante é iniciar um pipeline CDC sobre uma tabela que já contém dados.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Existing Table:
10 million records
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Precisamos carregar esse estado inicial.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Depois, precisamos acompanhar as alterações que ocorrem enquanto o snapshot está sendo produzido.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma arquitetura CDC deve garantir uma transição consistente entre:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;INITIAL SNAPSHOT
       |
       v
CONTINUOUS CHANGES
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Debezium oferece mecanismos específicos para esse cenário.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas o comportamento depende do conector, do modo de snapshot e da configuração.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Não devemos implementar uma carga inicial independente e simplesmente iniciar a leitura do WAL depois, sem estabelecer uma fronteira consistente entre as duas operações.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Isso pode causar perdas ou duplicidades.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  24. Schema Evolution em CDC
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agora imagine que o banco operacional adiciona uma coluna:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight sql"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;ALTER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;TABLE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pedidos&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;ADD&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;COLUMN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;canal_venda&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;VARCHAR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;O evento CDC poderá passar a conter essa informação.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas o pipeline Spark possui um schema definido.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Se não houver uma estratégia de evolução, o novo campo poderá ser ignorado ou causar incompatibilidades, dependendo da implementação.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Precisamos planejar:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolução do schema na origem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serialização dos eventos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compatibilidade no Schema Registry, quando utilizado.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolução do parsing Spark.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolução da tabela de destino.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contratos com consumidores.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma alteração no banco operacional pode afetar toda a cadeia analítica.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Esse é um exemplo claro da importância dos Data Contracts estudados na Parte 14.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  25. Schema Registry
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em arquiteturas de eventos, um Schema Registry pode ajudar a gerenciar schemas e regras de compatibilidade.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceitualmente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;EVENT PRODUCER
      |
      v
SCHEMA VALIDATION
      |
      v
KAFKA TOPIC
      |
      v
SPARK CONSUMER
      |
      v
SCHEMA RESOLUTION
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Dependendo do ecossistema, podemos utilizar formatos como:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avro.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protobuf.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JSON Schema.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas o Schema Registry não garante automaticamente que todos os consumidores estejam semanticamente compatíveis.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ele ajuda a gerenciar a estrutura e determinadas regras de evolução.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As regras de negócio continuam exigindo contratos e validações próprias.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  26. Replay e recuperação
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma vantagem importante do Kafka é permitir releitura de eventos ainda disponíveis conforme as políticas de retenção.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine que uma transformação Spark possuía um bug.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Depois da correção, talvez precisemos reprocessar os eventos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceitualmente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;KAFKA EVENT LOG
       |
       v
REPLAY
       |
       v
CORRECTED SPARK PIPELINE
       |
       v
REBUILT ANALYTICAL TABLE
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Mas replay exige planejamento.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Precisamos saber:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quais offsets representam o intervalo desejado.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se os eventos ainda estão disponíveis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se o destino deve ser reconstruído ou atualizado.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Como evitar duplicidades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Como preservar a ordem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Como validar o resultado.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Também não devemos apagar checkpoints indiscriminadamente para forçar um replay.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Isso pode causar efeitos inesperados no destino.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma estratégia segura pode utilizar uma nova consulta, um checkpoint separado e uma área de reconstrução controlada.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  27. Retenção Kafka não é retenção analítica
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Kafka pode reter eventos por tempo, tamanho ou políticas específicas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas não devemos tratá-lo automaticamente como armazenamento histórico permanente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine que o tópico possui retenção de sete dias.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Se um pipeline ficar indisponível por dez dias, determinados eventos podem não estar mais disponíveis.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Isso pode comprometer a recuperação.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Portanto, precisamos alinhar:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;KAFKA RETENTION
       |
       v
MAXIMUM RECOVERY WINDOW
       |
       v
PIPELINE SLA
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Para requisitos de histórico e auditoria, podemos persistir eventos brutos em uma camada de armazenamento durável.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Essa camada pode servir como base para reprocessamentos posteriores.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  28. Observabilidade de CDC
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma arquitetura CDC possui vários pontos de falha.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;POSTGRESQL
    |
    v
DEBEZIUM
    |
    v
KAFKA
    |
    v
SPARK
    |
    v
LAKEHOUSE
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Precisamos monitorar cada camada.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  PostgreSQL
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retenção de WAL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replication slots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lag de replicação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uso de armazenamento.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disponibilidade.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Debezium / Kafka Connect
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Estado do conector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Erros de captura.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progresso do snapshot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Falhas de serialização.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Kafka
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retenção.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disponibilidade de brokers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partições.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produção e consumo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lag, conforme o consumidor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Spark
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Duração dos microbatches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taxa de entrada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taxa de processamento.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Checkpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Falhas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backlog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Lakehouse
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tempo de MERGE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quantidade de arquivos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compactação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualidade.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistência.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Freshness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma aplicação Spark saudável não significa que toda a cadeia CDC esteja saudável.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  29. Latência ponta a ponta
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em uma arquitetura CDC, a latência relevante geralmente começa na alteração da origem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceitualmente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Database Commit
      |
      v
CDC Capture
      |
      v
Kafka Publish
      |
      v
Spark Processing
      |
      v
Lakehouse Commit
      |
      v
Consumer Availability
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Podemos definir:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;[&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  \text{End-to-End Latency}
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  \text{Availability Time}
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;\text{Source Commit Time}&lt;br&gt;
]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Essa métrica precisa utilizar timestamps confiáveis e semântica bem definida.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O timestamp de processamento do Spark, isoladamente, não mede toda a latência da cadeia.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Também precisamos distinguir latência média de percentis como P95 e P99.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma média baixa pode esconder eventos que demoram muito mais do que o esperado.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


  30. Data Quality em eventos CDC
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nem todo evento recebido deve ser aplicado automaticamente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Precisamos validar:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identificador do registro.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tipo de operação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Estrutura do payload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Versão da alteração.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Campos obrigatórios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regras de negócio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compatibilidade de schema.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Por exemplo:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_validos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_normalizados&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isNotNull&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;operacao&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Essa é apenas uma validação inicial.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em produção, precisamos diferenciar:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eventos válidos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eventos inválidos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tombstones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eventos de controle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alterações incompatíveis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Também precisamos preservar os dados necessários para investigação.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Descartar silenciosamente eventos CDC pode comprometer a consistência do destino.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  31. Laboratório local: simulando CDC sem Kafka
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agora vamos construir um exemplo executável em PySpark.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O objetivo é compreender a lógica de aplicação incremental sem depender de PostgreSQL, Kafka ou Debezium.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vamos simular eventos com:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identificador.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Versão de origem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Primeiro, criamos os eventos.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pyspark.sql&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;SparkSession&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pyspark.sql&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;functions&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pyspark.sql&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Window&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pyspark.sql.types&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;StructType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;LongType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;StringType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;DecimalType&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;decimal&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Decimal&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;spark&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;SparkSession&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;master&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;local[*]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;appName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;CDCLab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getOrCreate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;schema&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;LongType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;operacao&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StringType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StringType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;DecimalType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StructField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;LongType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;101&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;CRIADO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Decimal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;150.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;101&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;PAGO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Decimal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;150.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;102&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;CRIADO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Decimal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;230.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;101&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;ENVIADO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Decimal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;150.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;102&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;103&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;CRIADO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Decimal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;99.90&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;101&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;PAGO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Decimal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;150.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;df_eventos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;spark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createDataFrame&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;schema&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;schema&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;df_eventos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;show&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;truncate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Observe que incluímos propositalmente um evento antigo repetido do pedido 101.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  32. Selecionando o estado mais recente
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agora queremos identificar o último evento lógico de cada pedido.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;janela&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;Window&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;partitionBy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;orderBy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;desc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_recentes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;df_eventos&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;withColumn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;rn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;row_number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;over&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;janela&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;rn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;drop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;rn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_recentes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;show&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;truncate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Como os eventos duplicados do pedido 101 possuem a mesma versão e o mesmo conteúdo, não há conflito de estado nesse exemplo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em produção, versões iguais com conteúdos diferentes precisam ser tratadas como inconsistência ou resolvidas por uma regra explícita.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  33. Aplicando exclusões
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agora separamos os registros cujo último evento representa delete.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;registros_ativos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_recentes&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;operacao&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;valor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;registros_excluidos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;eventos_recentes&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;F&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;operacao&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;pedido_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;source_version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Podemos visualizar:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;registros_ativos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;show&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;registros_excluidos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;show&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;O estado ativo esperado é:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pedido_id = 101
status = ENVIADO

pedido_id = 103
status = CRIADO
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;O pedido 102 foi excluído logicamente da visão ativa.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Esse laboratório reconstrói o estado final a partir de todo o conjunto de eventos disponível.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ele não representa, sozinho, uma implementação incremental transacional de produção.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  34. Por que manter o histórico de alterações?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Uma tabela de estado atual responde:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Qual é a situação do pedido agora?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas não responde necessariamente:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Como o pedido chegou a esse estado?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Por isso, muitas arquiteturas mantêm duas representações.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event History&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Preserva as alterações recebidas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current State&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Representa o estado mais recente de cada entidade.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceitualmente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;                  CDC EVENTS
                      |
             +--------+--------+
             |                 |
             v                 v
       EVENT HISTORY       CURRENT STATE
             |                 |
             v                 v
          AUDIT           ANALYTICS
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Essa separação pode facilitar:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Auditoria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replay.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconstrução de tabelas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Análises temporais.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas o histórico precisa de políticas de retenção, privacidade e acesso.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  35. Uma arquitetura de referência para produção
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vamos reunir as principais decisões.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;                  OPERATIONAL SYSTEM
                         |
                         v
                     POSTGRESQL
                         |
                         v
                    LOGICAL WAL
                         |
                         v
                      DEBEZIUM
                         |
                         v
                    KAFKA TOPICS
                         |
                         v
                 SPARK STREAMING
                         |
                         v
                 CONTRACT VALIDATION
                         |
                         v
                   CDC NORMALIZATION
                         |
                         v
                 ORDERING / DEDUP
                         |
                         v
                    QUALITY GATES
                         |
              +----------+----------+
              |                     |
              v                     v
          VALID EVENTS         QUARANTINE
              |
              v
         RAW EVENT HISTORY
              |
              v
         INCREMENTAL MERGE
              |
              v
         LAKEHOUSE TABLE
              |
              v
          SQL / BI / ML
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Em uma implementação real, algumas dessas responsabilidades podem ser reorganizadas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Por exemplo, podemos persistir o histórico bruto antes das validações de negócio, preservando eventos para auditoria e reprocessamento.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O desenho depende dos requisitos de segurança, recuperação e consistência.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  36. Quando CDC não é necessário?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CDC é poderoso, mas introduz complexidade.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Talvez não seja necessário quando:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A tabela é pequena.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A atualização é pouco frequente.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;O SLA permite cargas diárias.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Não existem deletes relevantes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;O sistema de origem oferece APIs incrementais confiáveis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;O custo operacional do CDC supera seus benefícios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Em alguns cenários, uma carga incremental por timestamp bem implementada pode ser suficiente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A decisão deve considerar:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequência de mudanças.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Latência.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Custo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complexidade.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Garantias de consistência.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacidade operacional da equipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A arquitetura mais sofisticada nem sempre é a melhor arquitetura.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  37. Erros comuns em pipelines CDC
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Alguns erros merecem atenção especial.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Utilizar timestamp como única garantia de ordenação.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pode não representar a sequência real das alterações.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ignorar eventos de delete.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O destino pode manter registros inexistentes na origem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Confundir tombstone Kafka com delete CDC.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;São conceitos relacionados, mas diferentes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Aplicar MERGE sem controle de versão.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Eventos antigos podem sobrescrever estados novos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Não monitorar replication slots.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O WAL pode crescer e comprometer o PostgreSQL.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Não planejar snapshot inicial.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Podem ocorrer lacunas ou duplicidades entre carga inicial e streaming.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Não definir política de replay.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Falhas podem exigir reconstruções difíceis.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assumir exactly-once em qualquer destino.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As garantias dependem da arquitetura completa.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Não versionar schemas.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mudanças na origem podem quebrar consumidores.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Não preservar histórico quando necessário.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Isso dificulta auditoria e reprocessamento.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  38. Como eu avaliaria uma arquitetura CDC
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Antes de colocar um pipeline em produção, faria perguntas como:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Qual é o banco de origem?
          |
          v
Como as alterações são capturadas?
          |
          v
Como funciona o snapshot inicial?
          |
          v
Qual é a chave do registro?
          |
          v
Como preservamos a ordem?
          |
          v
Como tratamos duplicidades?
          |
          v
Como tratamos DELETE?
          |
          v
Como controlamos versões?
          |
          v
Como garantimos idempotência?
          |
          v
Como fazemos replay?
          |
          v
Qual é a retenção necessária?
          |
          v
Como monitoramos lag?
          |
          v
Como validamos a consistência final?
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Essas perguntas precisam ser respondidas antes de considerar a arquitetura pronta.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  39. A principal lição deste capítulo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Apache Kafka, Debezium e Spark Structured Streaming permitem construir pipelines incrementais capazes de acompanhar mudanças em sistemas transacionais.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mas a complexidade principal não está apenas em transportar eventos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ela está em preservar corretamente a semântica das alterações.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Precisamos compreender:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Origem das mudanças.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ordenação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chaves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Duplicidades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deletes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Snapshots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Versões.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Checkpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Idempotência.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recuperação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualidade.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O princípio mais importante é:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CDC não é apenas capturar mudanças. É reconstruir e manter corretamente o estado dos dados a partir dessas mudanças.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  40. Como penso hoje
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Quando avalio uma plataforma que promete dados em tempo quase real, não pergunto apenas:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Qual é a latência do Kafka?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Quero saber:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Como as mudanças são capturadas?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qual é a consistência do snapshot inicial?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Como eventos fora de ordem são tratados?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Como o destino evita atualizações antigas?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Como deletes são preservados?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;O que acontece após uma falha?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Como os eventos podem ser reprocessados?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Como monitoramos a cadeia inteira?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Como validamos a consistência entre origem e destino?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Essas perguntas representam a diferença entre um pipeline que transporta mensagens e uma arquitetura incremental confiável.&lt;/p&gt;




